# Single simulation source of truth

## Rule

- Episode semantics must follow: one episode = one canonical simulation rollout.
- `backend/simulation/run_simulation.py::run_simulation` is the canonical simulation source for episode-level world-state generation.
- Train, eval, and render paths must use the same canonical simulation outputs and must not diverge into parallel simulation implementations.

## Required artifact contract

- Episode-level runs must produce/consume `simulation.state_types.SimulationStateSeries`.
- If an interface currently returns partial state only, refactor plans must include convergence to `SimulationStateSeries` instead of adding new ad-hoc state types.

## Forbidden patterns

- Re-running a separate simulation path for export/visualization when the episode simulation output is already available.
- Maintaining duplicated simulation logic across script-specific helper functions.
- Computing reward-critical world signals outside canonical simulation ownership.

## Scope declaration

- Long-term architecture target is hierarchical mission-level control over OBC low-level control.
- Direct low-level torque-learning interfaces are interim experimental tools and must be documented as such.
